    "histoire_heading": "Our story",
    "histoire_text": "Founded in 2013 in Paris, NO MORE WASTE is a humanitarian association fighting food waste. It has gradually expanded across France (Nantes, Marseille, Limoges), then internationally (Naples, Porto, Dublin). Every day, trucks leave the head office to collect unsold commercial goods and products nearing their expiry date from individuals, before redistributing them wherever needed. Beyond collection, the association offers its members a range of services to help avoid waste, share and save money: anti-waste advice, cooking classes, car sharing, skill exchanges between individuals, repairs, house-sitting...",
    "benevoles_heading": "Our volunteers",
    "benevoles_text": "Drivers, cooks, plumbers, electricians... more than 200 volunteers keep the association running day to day: they carry out pickups and delivery routes, and run the services offered to members. Everyone offers their skills and signs up for the slots that suit them.",
    "adherents_heading": "Our members",
    "adherents_text": "Are you a shop owner? By joining NO MORE WASTE, you donate your unsold goods instead of throwing them away, and in return enjoy the association's services (cooking classes, car sharing, repairs...) for a small annual fee.",

